# Local daemon config (may contain secrets; use config.example.json as template)
/config.json

/heros-data/
/.heros-data/

# Compiled binaries (build outputs — never version these)
#
# `go build ./cmd/...` drops a binary named after its directory into the REPO ROOT, so this used to be
# one line per command — and it fell behind every time a command was added. When this was written there
# were eight untracked Mach-O files in the root and four of them matched no rule at all.
#
# So the shape is ignored rather than the instances. Every one of those binaries is an EXTENSIONLESS
# FILE AT THE ROOT, and nothing that belongs at the root is: source lives in directories, and the few
# extensionless root files there are get named below.
#
# ⚠️ The trade, stated: a NEW legitimate extensionless root file would be ignored silently until
# somebody adds it here. That surface is small and rare, and it is the price of not having to remember
# this file every time a command is added — which is the thing that already failed.
/*
!/*/
!/*.*
!/Makefile
!/LICENSE
!/NOTICE
/bin/
*.exe

# Crash dumps and local scratch
*.stackdump

# Deliberately-weakened compose spec written by scripts/discovery_sandbox_redcheck.py. It is removed
# in a finally block, but if the red-check is killed mid-run the leftover must never be committable:
# it is a copy of the discovery worker spec with a least-privilege guarantee removed.
/deploy/.redcheck-compose.discovery.yml

# Local runtime state (must never be versioned)
/internal/cliagent/.heros/

# Go build cache (local; not for version control)
/.gocache/

# Local-only business strategy (do not commit)
/docs/business/evaluation-and-monetization.md
/docs/business/pricing-plan.md
.parity/

# ── install-smoke staging (scripts/install_smoke.py) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 🔴 THIS RULE WAS MISSING, AND TWO PLACES IN THE CODEBASE ALREADY ASSUMED IT WAS HERE.
#
#   scripts/install_smoke.py:642        "Staging inside the repository (gitignored) keeps every mount
#                                        on a path Docker actually shares."
#   internal/distribution/handwritten.go  "The skipped directories are the ones whose contents are NOT
#                                        committed: … the install-smoke staging area."
#
# Both sentences were false. `.smoke/` was tracked, and because the script stages each run in a FRESH
# `run-<random>` directory (tempfile.mkdtemp), every invocation added a new copy of the release
# binaries it builds. Ten run directories reached HEAD carrying 169 files and 672 MiB — 97% of the
# repository by size, against roughly 19 MiB of actual source.
#
# It went unnoticed because nothing reads these paths back: CI regenerates the staging area from
# scratch on every run (.github/workflows/install-smoke.yml), and the P20 evidence doc quotes a
# `.smoke/...` path only inside a pasted terminal transcript, which is the evidence itself.
#
# The cost was invisible until `heros push-source` archived the tracked tree and printed its size.
# A repository does not complain about being large.
.smoke/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Demo binaries built at the repo root by `go build -o <name> ./cmd/<name>`.
#
# They are build output, not source: ~20MB each, they rebuild in seconds, and a committed one is a
# binary nobody reviews sitting in every clone forever. The list is explicit rather than a glob so an
# actual source file named after a command cannot be ignored by accident.
#
# ⚠️ authoringhermes, oaxhermes, p13hermes, p14hermes and p15hermes are ALREADY TRACKED from earlier
# phases (~86MB between them). Ignoring a path does not untrack it. Removing them is a separate,
# deliberate change against those phases' history, not a side effect of this one.
/p55demo
/p55hermes
/p6demo
/p6hermes
/p21hermes

# The per-phase hermes runners (cmd/*hermes). Each is a ~18MB Mach-O left behind by `go build`, and
# `git add -A` sweeps them in silently: the list above was already one build ahead of the tree. Listed
# explicitly rather than as a glob, so a NEW binary at the root is still a thing someone has to look at.
/authoringhermes
/oaxhermes
/p7hermes
/p8hermes
/p9hermes
/p12hermes
/p13hermes
/p14hermes
/p15hermes
/p16hermes

# P11 CLI local run store (customer-side; never committed) + release output
/.heros/
/dist/

# ── Generated by deploy/scripts/up.sh (`make deploy-up`) ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 🔴 These are the ONLY files under deploy/ that ever hold a real credential. Every other file there
# documents NAMES only and says so in its own header. They are generated once, on a first install, at
# 0600, and the script refuses to rewrite them — so the risk is not that they change, it is that
# `git add -A` sweeps them in on the commit after a deploy. A committed credential outlives the moment
# it was valid, and it ships.
#
# Listed by exact path rather than as `deploy/.env*`, so that a NEW deploy/.env.* file is something a
# human has to look at instead of something that disappears silently — the same posture the root-binary
# rules above take.
/deploy/.env.local
/deploy/config/config.json
